Enable NVMe as a built-in driver (CONFIG_NVME_CORE=y + CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME=y)
across the QEMU Linux defconfigs so guests can use a virtio/PCIe NVMe device
without loading a module from an initramfs.

  - arm64 (aarch64):  BLK_DEV_NVME was =m, switch to =y
  - riscv64:          BLK_DEV_NVME was =m, switch to =y
  - x86_64:           BLK_DEV_NVME was unset, add =y
  - loongarch64:      already =y in loongson64_defconfig, no change needed

Generated with `git diff` against the Linux source tree at ref
74fe02ce122a6103f207d29fafc8b3a53de6abaf (after 0001-enable-sbi-v01.patch).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
index d905a0777..0c064a83f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/defconfig
@@ -311,7 +311,8 @@ CONFIG_HBMC_AM654=m
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
 CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NBD=m
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK=y
-CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME=m
+CONFIG_NVME_CORE=y
+CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME=y
 CONFIG_NVME_APPLE=m
 CONFIG_QCOM_COINCELL=m
 CONFIG_QCOM_FASTRPC=m
